#: ../../../source/Capabilities/About-Perception.rst:12
msgid ""
"Perception capabilities help your robot to understand and interpret the "
"world using sensors like cameras, LIDAR, depth sensors, and RADAR. This "
"article summarizes ROS developer tools and guidance available to help with "
"perception."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/About-Perception.rst:26
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/About-Perception.rst:29
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Capabilities/About-Perception.rst:31
msgid ""
"Perception capabilities are how your robot sees the world. They enable your "
"robot to process data from a range of sensors, such as cameras, bump "
"sensors, and LIDAR sensors, and turn that into information the robot can use "
"to plan and control its actions. This includes sensor fusion (combining data "
"from multiple sensors into a unified view of the world)."
msgstr ""

